    "patchSets": [
        {
            "number": 1,
            "revision": "2e7aaa116a0ee6e7fafbbedaa54efcf45cde6cf1",
            "parents": [
                "f4b0322f14513171af7531807d56373204224eb3"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/41/84641/1",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Ed Tanous",
                "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                "username": "edtanous"
            },
            "createdOn": 1761349849,
            "author": {
                "name": "Ed Tanous",
                "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                "username": "edtanous"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "There is already a Metric.Value that has Count as a type.  I think we're going to need clarity on when Metric.Value and when Metric.Counts should be used.  Is it worth adding something to a README.md in the Metric subdirectory?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "For counters I would argue that this should always be used unless you need backward compatibility.  There's 2 counters noted in the existing API, RebootCount, RebootCountWithFailure.  Neither of those will see a fast-changing count to where this interface would be a solution, so we could decide if those should be moved in the future."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "How is this different than Metric.Value, which also has counters?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Metric.Value requires:\n\n1. A path per metric\n2. A PropertiesChanged event on every update\n3. To select some kind of polling interval.\n\n\nThe proposed interface has all that, and the advantages (without comparison) are listed in the description for this."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "/s/proposed interface has all that/proposed interface has NONE of that/g"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Count.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 2,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Is this arbitrary or well-known?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Count.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 2,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Arbitrary.  Where there's agreement on a counter name (like for PCIe, etc) we will document them here, but the goal is that this can include any counter without imposing limits in documentation."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Count.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Do this as opposed to an association? (Personally I prefer this approach over association, but I supposed Metric.Value paths use associations)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Count.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "We don't want regularly changing things in the inventory namespace.  Please make this an association or a clear X -> Y transformation for the path."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Count.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "The goal here was to avoid needing to do a complex mapper lookup to get the counters for a given path.  If we have, say, 100 counters for a given inventory item, that's now a lot of lookups.\n\n> regularly changing things \n\nThese intentionally have no properties, so they're not \"changing\".  Is there a concern about other signals where this would change?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Count.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Can this be a dict instead?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Count.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I intentionally didn't want it to be a dict, because the general usage is to enumerate and populate.  It could be a dict if we wanted (they're the same), but I didn't want to imply that there was an expected order/lookupability."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Count.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Should this be updated each time a counter is added?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Count.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why aren't these enumerations?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Count.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "So that additional newly added properties do not cause failures.  Not all services will require all values."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Metric/Count.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "> So that additional newly added properties do not cause failures. Not all services will require all values.\n\nCan you elaborate?  I don't know what kind of failures you're envisioning being caused.\n\nGenerally we've made a big push to \"no arbitrary strings that isn't used exclusively by humans\" in PDI.  It isn't clear to me what is special about these ones."
                }
            ],
